{"paper": "2022-Tier1-01-Dec-2022-Shift1.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 25, "tagged_count": 25, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "A dishonest merchant sells goods at a 12.5% loss on the cost price, but uses 28 g weight instead of 36 g. What is his percentage profit or loss?", "options": [{"text": "6.25% loss", "added": false}, {"text": "12.5% gain", "added": false}, {"text": "18.75% gain", "added": false}, {"text": "10.5% loss", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "dishonest-dealer", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "The HCF of two numbers is 12. Which one of the following can never be their LCM?", "options": [{"text": "72", "added": false}, {"text": "60", "added": false}, {"text": "90", "added": false}, {"text": "84", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-numbers", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "Two circles touch each other externally at P. AB is a direct common tangent to the two circles, A and B are points of contact, and ∠PAB = 40° . The measure of ∠ ABP is:", "options": [{"text": "45°", "added": false}, {"text": "55°", "added": false}, {"text": "50°", "added": false}, {"text": "40°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "The mean proportion of 169 and 144 is:", "options": [{"text": "156", "added": false}, {"text": "147", "added": false}, {"text": "126", "added": false}, {"text": "165", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "proportion", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "The length and breadth of a rectangle are increased by 8% and 5%, respectively. By how much percentage will the area of the rectangle increase?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "successive-change", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "46", "added": false}, {"text": "14", "added": false}, {"text": "8", "added": false}, {"text": "50", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "In a 1500 m race, Anil beats Bakul by 150 m and in the same race Bakul beats Charles by 75 m. By what distance does Anil beat Charles?", "options": [{"text": "217.50 m", "added": false}, {"text": "200.15 m", "added": false}, {"text": "293.50 m", "added": false}, {"text": "313.75 m", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "basic-tsd", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "₹2,500, when invested for 8 years at a given rate of simple interest per year, amounted to ₹3,725 on maturity. What was the rate of simple interest that was paid per annum?", "options": [{"text": "6%", "added": false}, {"text": "6.125%", "added": false}, {"text": "6.25%", "added": false}, {"text": "5.875%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-formula", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "196", "added": false}, {"text": "194", "added": false}, {"text": "192", "added": false}, {"text": "190", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "The batting average for 27 innings of a cricket player is 47 runs. His highest score in an innings exceeds his lowest score by 157 runs. If these two innings are excluded, the average score of the remaining 25 innings is 42 runs. Find his highest score in an innings.", "options": [{"text": "176", "added": false}, {"text": "188", "added": false}, {"text": "186", "added": false}, {"text": "174", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "P and Q can complete a project in 15 days and 10 days, respectively. They started doing the work together, but after 2 days, Q had to leave and P alone completed the remaining work. In how many days was the whole work completed?", "options": [{"text": "11", "added": false}, {"text": "12", "added": false}, {"text": "13", "added": false}, {"text": "10", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "The pie chart given below shows the number of truck sold by 8 different companies. The total number of truck sold by all these 8 companies are 4000. Number of truck sold by a particular company is shown as a percent of total number of truck sold by all these 8 companies. The number of trucks sold by B, C, F and H is how much percent less than the number of trucks sold by all these 8 companies?", "options": [{"text": "46 percent", "added": false}, {"text": "22 percent", "added": false}, {"text": "34 percent", "added": false}, {"text": "14 percent", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "pie-chart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "30", "added": false}, {"text": "25", "added": false}, {"text": "23", "added": false}, {"text": "28", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "In a right-angled triangle PQR, right-angled at Q, the length of the side PR is 17 units, length of the base QR is 8 units, and length of the side PQ is 15 units. If ∠ RPQ = α, then sinα + cosα is:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "triangles", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "If , then what is the value of k?", "options": [{"text": "119", "added": false}, {"text": "128", "added": false}, {"text": "24", "added": false}, {"text": "109", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "expression-values", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "The circumference of the two circles is 198 cm and 352 cm respectively. What is the difference between their radii?", "options": [{"text": "45 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "16.5 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "49.5 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "24.5 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "circle-sector-ring", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "Radius of a circle is 10 cm. Angle made by chord AB at the centre of this circle is 60 degree. What is the length of this chord?", "options": [{"text": "40 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "20 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "30 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "10 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "circle-theorems", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "920", "added": false}, {"text": "750", "added": false}, {"text": "650", "added": false}, {"text": "860", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "The table given below shows the number of spoon manufactured by five factories. What are the ratio of number of spoon manufactured by P to the number of spoon manufactured by R?", "options": [{"text": "3 : 2", "added": false}, {"text": "2 : 3", "added": false}, {"text": "14 : 1", "added": false}, {"text": "1 : 3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "10 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "7.13 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "13.20 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "11.13 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "The value of tan2 θ + cot2 θ − sec2 θ cosec2 θ is:", "options": [{"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "−2", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "1/2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "ratios-and-tables", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "If , then what is the value of p?", "options": [{"text": "–119", "added": false}, {"text": "–129", "added": false}, {"text": "119", "added": false}, {"text": "129", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "expression-values", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "Riya could not decide between discount of 30% or two successive discounts of 25% and 5%, both given on shopping of ₹3,840. What is the difference between both the discounts?", "options": [{"text": "₹44", "added": false}, {"text": "₹48", "added": false}, {"text": "₹42", "added": false}, {"text": "₹46", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "successive-discounts", "key_answer": null}]}